{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1399452-hardtech-ftl","id":1399452,"title":"Hardtech FTL?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-27T18:26:29-07:00","id":1399452,"title":"Hardtech FTL?","content":"So, is there any example of Hardtech FTL in the setting, either from Nova's or Aliens? It seems at this point that FTL is restricted either to psychic powers (leviathan/teleporters) or novas with Warp.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T18:31:56-07:00","id":1399456,"title":"","content":"Novas created Nova and Q tech using Warp, that is basically a Hyperdrive, as it takes time to travel and don\u2019t use real space to travel.<br /> <br /> Warp Speed (like StarTrek Warp) have no equivalent in Nova powers, as they still obey at this basic law of physics, but it\u2019s still FTL travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T18:37:06-07:00","id":1399459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1399452-hardtech-ftl#post1399452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems at this point that FTL is restricted either to psychic powers (leviathan/teleporters) or novas with Warp.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is exactly an underlying assumption of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T20:18:19-07:00","id":1399483,"title":"","content":"I actually like that assumption about Aeon. Distinguishes it from more conventional sci-fi settings.<br /> <br /> My friend was really into the idea of combining Star Trek and Aeon, but if I did that at all it would be an alternate universe. The main Aeon timeline has its own unique flavor and I wouldn\u2019t want to compromise that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T00:06:02-07:00","id":1399524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1399452-hardtech-ftl?p=1399456#post1399456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Novas created Nova and Q tech using Warp, that is basically a Hyperdrive, as it takes time to travel and don\u2019t use real space to travel.<br /> <br /> Warp Speed (like StarTrek Warp) have no equivalent in Nova powers, as they still obey at this basic law of physics, but it\u2019s still FTL travel.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So we could use the same process that takes nova tech and eventually makes it conventional tech for their warp? Go from Quantum tech, to nova Tech, to conventional tech. (Granted, that'd probably take a long, long time.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T03:00:53-07:00","id":1399540,"title":"","content":"@NewK probably several centuries at least","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T04:10:04-07:00","id":1399556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1399452-hardtech-ftl?p=1399524#post1399524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we could use the same process that takes nova tech and eventually makes it conventional tech for their warp? Go from Quantum tech, to nova Tech, to conventional tech. (Granted, that'd probably take a long, long time.).</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be done, yes. It would still be FTL based off Quantum powers, just like the Leviathan is teleportation tech based of psionic powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T06:23:58-07:00","id":1399583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1399452-hardtech-ftl?p=1399556#post1399556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It could be done, yes. It would still be FTL based off Quantum powers, just like the Leviathan is teleportation tech based of psionic powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense, but generated a few questions not related to FTL drives.<br /> <br /> Is Hyperfusion and Gravcrystals considered Based on Quantum powers? Both were invented by novas, and sure it\u2019s not Natural, but after some time it just became \u201cregular\u201d (common and nobody think it\u2019s corrupted, as they think about other novatech).<br /> <br /> Also, the Coalition ship has artificial gravity (I suppose), is it made with Gravcrystals or is it a complete different tech, and is it considered based on quantum powers even without \u201cnovas\u201d in their races?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T07:45:49-07:00","id":1399594,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz maybe the Coalition space ark doesn\u2019t have artificial gravity, or at least it\u2019s not powered by Gravcrystals. I don\u2019t think any of the Coalition races (except maybe a few of the Progenitors?) have access to quantum powers or novatech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T09:27:54-07:00","id":1399607,"title":"","content":"They were naturally Psionics, but they removed this from their DNA to avoid becoming a hive mind (as a part of their society did).<br /> <br /> But yes, that is exactly the point. If they have gravity (and by the arts I would say yes), it can be caused by the constant acceleration (what should make their ships 70km tall, not long) or by an artificial gravity device (similar to Gravcrystals).<br /> <br /> As I see, once it\u2019s core tech / advanced super science, it stops being powered by quantum/psi and start to be part of the way Reality works. It still use quantum or psi, but it\u2019s not properly a quantum power it\u2019s like an exploit of reality rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T10:46:00-07:00","id":1399619,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz hmmm, good point. Maybe one of the member races of the Coalition thousands of years ago invented a novatech device similar to Gravcrystals? A device that allowed the Coalition space arks to use artificial gravity without being several dozen miles tall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T17:48:42-07:00","id":1400217,"title":"","content":"Cool discussion! <br /> <br /> In defense of Joe Hologram: the space programs of Earth had invented well, space travel IRL and in Aeon without the help of any superhumans (presumably) and so I'd be interested to see what impact the Unity Age has on conventional technologies. <br /> <br /> For instance, what would Orgotek's Lumen Division do with the designs of a solar sail ship? How would space age tech influence plans and designs that we have, irl, right now? <br /> <br /> Would someone have tried to put together a ship resembling The Orion Project? (Controlled nuclear explosions for propulsion, short explanation). <br /> <br /> Would the baseline scientists observing a Upeo using the Warp mode be able to extrapolate the math for a working Alcubierre drive...? <br /> <br /> Also, what the hell are the Qin up to...? I could see them engaging in secret tests with a &quot;gravity drive&quot; similar to SW: NJO's Yuuzhan Vong...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25900-tritoninvestigator","name":"Tritoninvestigator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T18:38:52-07:00","id":1400228,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind the difference between core-tech, nova-tech, and Q-tech.<br /> <br /> Eufiber, for example, is the foundation of the OpNet. It's definitely core-tech. Gravcrystals' origin hasn't been specified, only that they're &quot;nova age technology&quot; developed in 2043. They <i>may</i> have been developed by a nova, but they're still core-tech. They probably would have been invented sooner or later, even without novas. Piezoelectric materials (which include some crystals!) are materials which translate mechanical stress into electrical charge. I imagine grav crystals are similar, but instead translate an electrical charge into a graviton field.<br /> <br /> \u00c6on's Science &amp; Technology division mostly cares about sweeping up Q-tech and nova-tech. Sometimes they'll grab core-tech if they know a nova was involved, just in case, but for stuff like eufiber and grav crystals, they're too ubiquitous, and that ubiquity almost certainly would have shown a problem in the last ~80-100 years if there was one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T20:22:46-07:00","id":1400239,"title":"","content":"I can't quote page number but I've been reading through my print copy of Distant Worlds and it mentions the Qin having Biotech Grav Crystals. <br /> Granted the could have developed them since contact with humans, but I feel like, since they colonized worlds via sub-light travel more than 10,000 years ago, the probably had grav crystals. Even at 99% light speed, traveling 58 light years, they would experience ~25 years time. 25 years is a LONG time to be in microgravity. Hell, 6 months is a long time to be in microgravity.<br /> Even their closest colony, at 3.5 light years, would take a little over 4 years real time, and over a year and a half relative time on ship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T21:04:35-07:00","id":1400240,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4\" data-vbnamecard=\"4\">IanWatson</a> good point<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25900-tritoninvestigator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25900\" data-vbnamecard=\"25900\">Tritoninvestigator</a> very cool post. Just wish I knew more about astrophysics so I could respond more intelligently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T11:53:49-07:00","id":1400367,"title":"","content":"<span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> for pretty much all of the lockdown, I've been *heavily* into the Youbute channels SFIA (Science and Futurism with Isaac Arthur), John Michael Gautier and PBS science - highly recommend checking some of them out re: hard tech inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25900-tritoninvestigator","name":"Tritoninvestigator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T11:57:51-07:00","id":1400368,"title":"","content":"Awesome \ud83d\ude0a. Is Marshall McLuhan Futurism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T12:04:22-07:00","id":1400372,"title":"","content":"About one of the highest hardtech levels, we have the Hexers, with their inertialess technology. If there's a way to lower inertia to zero, perhaps there could be FTL implications, a l\u00e0 Lensman inertialess drive (if anybody know what I am talking about, this one is Jurassic). At the very least getting pretty close to the speed of light would be much, much cheaper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T14:17:44-07:00","id":1400395,"title":"","content":"Lensman still had Lumineferous Ether, IIRC; and the speed limit of a spacecraft in that setting was set by the thrust of its engines vs. the drag of the Ether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T16:13:46-07:00","id":1400415,"title":"","content":"<span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I'm not an expert, but I think he had what could be considered futuristic philosophy? I'm BSing at this point - but given his historical timeframe, maybe Mercer gave him some ideas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25900-tritoninvestigator","name":"Tritoninvestigator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T16:39:58-07:00","id":1400418,"title":"","content":"Makes me think of Dune and the stranglehold the Spacing Guild and Navigators (insert teleporters/clairs here) held on the empire for most of the novels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T16:55:16-07:00","id":1400419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tritoninvestigator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1399452-hardtech-ftl?p=1400415#post1400415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I'm not an expert, but I think he had what could be considered futuristic philosophy? I'm BSing at this point - but given his historical timeframe, maybe Mercer gave him some ideas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Marshall McLuhan lived (I think) in the Sixties, so it\u2019s very possible. (I like history \ud83d\ude0a.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T17:14:49-07:00","id":1400422,"title":"","content":"Can I just say that Dune would be an awesome thematic way to play a space opera Trinity game. Space Nobles and Great Houses and various organizations and a vast Imperium, soooooooo cool! <br /> <br /> Another awesome idea would be the Galactic Empire of the Foundation series by Isaac Asimov. Talents with some higher abilities would be great for the Second Foundation. Them or Superiors and such.<br /> <br /> Oh man, now I want to play in the Foundation universe. hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T17:29:57-07:00","id":1400426,"title":"","content":"Trinity would be perfect for Fading Suns and Dune!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 07-01-2020, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T21:27:42-07:00","id":1400454,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to leave my Snark here and say Trek isn't based on Hard Tech.. having all sorts of Random Q-tech being bolted to the ships that the crew barely understands would explain all the impossible effects for the Holodeck creating Sapient life for example. Or Teleporting to the wrong universe...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T01:13:16-07:00","id":1400471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1399452-hardtech-ftl?p=1400395#post1400395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lensman still had Lumineferous Ether, IIRC; and the speed limit of a spacecraft in that setting was set by the thrust of its engines vs. the drag of the Ether.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was not lumineferous ether, IIRC. It has been a long time, but just the random particles in the near-vacuum of space were enough to drag the ship. In fact, one random atom could stop the ship, or send it in any direction, since it was inertialess. So to keep the speed, there had to be a constant thrust, and the speed was based on the thrust vs the density of the vacuum. But, you see, this is the grandfather of the space opera, so the terminology of the epoch was it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T23:41:24-07:00","id":1400906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1399452-hardtech-ftl#post1399452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, is there any example of Hardtech FTL in the setting, either from Nova's or Aliens? It seems at this point that FTL is restricted either to psychic powers (leviathan/teleporters) or novas with Warp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. I'm completely certain a Nova could build a hardtech FTL drive, but it would be Quantum technology that only a nova could make, and not any sort of advanced super science. Basically, you need either psi or quantum powers to do any sort of FTL, including building an FTL drive. No matter how advanced humans or any other species get, FTL requires special powers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T09:22:16-07:00","id":1400962,"title":"","content":"I totally could see Nova built Quantum tech FTL technology that after thousands of iterations and millennia of work become 'mundane' in the sense that a baseline person could build it. Buuut that doesn't take away the fact that at its core its using the energies that novas use and such. This whole idea is similar to the concept of say the Iron Man armor. The first version requires Tony Stark to use, for this convo he is a Nova. The second version, after much work, can be personally designed by Tony for a baseline or Talent (such as Rhodey with War Machine armor). Even more versions and a version of said armor can be used by baselines. That said the version used by baselines and the most recent Tony specific armor are going to be quite different from each other. So the mundane available Quantum Drive engine and the Nova controlled Quantum Drive engine are gonna be verrrrrrry far in capability. <br /> <br /> This is just my opinion of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T11:50:14-07:00","id":1400982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1399452-hardtech-ftl?p=1400962#post1400962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I totally could see Nova built Quantum tech FTL technology that after thousands of iterations and millennia of work become 'mundane' in the sense that a baseline person could build it. Buuut that doesn't take away the fact that at its core its using the energies that novas use and such. This whole idea is similar to the concept of say the Iron Man armor. The first version requires Tony Stark to use, for this convo he is a Nova. The second version, after much work, can be personally designed by Tony for a baseline or Talent (such as Rhodey with War Machine armor). Even more versions and a version of said armor can be used by baselines. That said the version used by baselines and the most recent Tony specific armor are going to be quite different from each other. So the mundane available Quantum Drive engine and the Nova controlled Quantum Drive engine are gonna be verrrrrrry far in capability.<br /> <br /> This is just my opinion of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like Lord Heru says, it's my understanding (and correct me if I'm wrong) that the technology that Novas and Psions create can also be developed by baselines eventually, it just takes a loooooot more time. Also, Psions and Novas kind of &quot;cheat&quot; since they have access to exotic forms of energy, which solves the main issue with all these devices which is how to power them. So I imagine that for the &quot;Space Opera&quot; era of the continuum FTL technology would have advanced enough that baselines can create it. That said, Psions and Novas would still have access to the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T10:31:12-07:00","id":1401146,"title":"","content":"Specifically, TC:Aberrant will be including rules for \u201creverse engineering\u201d Nova-Tech, such that given enough time and effort an innovation created by a Nova can eventually be turned into something that's mass-produced and a ubiquitous part of society that for all practical purposes has nothing to do with Novas anymore. <br /> <br /> And yes, I could see Hard-tech FTL being developed in this manner: it <i>started out</i> as Q-Tech, but it's now available to anyone with the time and resources to build it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T18:43:07-07:00","id":1402163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1399452-hardtech-ftl?p=1401146#post1401146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically, TC:Aberrant will be including rules for \u201creverse engineering\u201d Nova-Tech, such that given enough time and effort an innovation created by a Nova can eventually be turned into something that's mass-produced and a ubiquitous part of society that for all practical purposes has nothing to do with Novas anymore.<br /> <br /> And yes, I could see Hard-tech FTL being developed in this manner: it <i>started out</i> as Q-Tech, but it's now available to anyone with the time and resources to build it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the closest anyone should get would be a prototype of some sort. You don't really want Trinity turning into Star Trek/Star Wars. But maybe somebody does build a prototype and... something goes wrong. And then you run Event Horizon in Trinity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T20:53:10-07:00","id":1402183,"title":"","content":"I'll grant that the reverse-engineered stuff isn't as effective as the original; and as such, the version of Hard-tech FTL that you get from reverse engineering Quantum FTL won't be as good (e.g., not as fast). I could see Hard-tech FTL being the poor man's FTL: it will get you to other star systems much faster than STL will, but it's slow enough that given a choice between that or having a psi or Nova transport you, you'll end up choosing the latter every time. <br /> <br /> So no, <i>not</i> Trinity turning into Star Trek or Star Wars; but not a monopoly on FTL by the teleporters either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T14:59:50-07:00","id":1402304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1399452-hardtech-ftl?p=1402183#post1402183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll grant that the reverse-engineered stuff isn't as effective as the original; and as such, the version of Hard-tech FTL that you get from reverse engineering Quantum FTL won't be as good (e.g., not as fast). I could see Hard-tech FTL being the poor man's FTL: it will get you to other star systems much faster than STL will, but it's slow enough that given a choice between that or having a psi or Nova transport you, you'll end up choosing the latter every time.<br /> <br /> So no, <i>not</i> Trinity turning into Star Trek or Star Wars; but not a monopoly on FTL by the teleporters either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Figure if you want to get somewhere quickly <i>and</i> safely, you'll use a Nova or a Psi. If you want to get somewhere quickly <i>or</i> safely you use a high-end hardtech FTL. If you want to get there cheaply (and possibly not at all) you go with low-end FTL and we run Trinity Event Horizon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T15:26:08-07:00","id":1402309,"title":"","content":"The above and maybe if you want to get between two highly visited locations along a path that has been trod a thousand times and so has little left unknown then you can use low-end FTL. The trade ships between planet a and planet b in systems that have been traveled for decades to centuries can make use of this tech with little difficulty. BUT, if one wants to go to planet c in another system then one should get a psion or a nova.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}